    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Blas">Blas</ref> 1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="388" ed="#liebermann"/>CXXI.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Blas_1.lnote.oe.1"/> We cwædon be þam blaserum ⁊ be þam morþslyhtum, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man dypte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Blas_1.lnote.oe.2"/> þone aþ be þryfealdum ⁊ myclade þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ordalysen, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hit gewege þry pund, ⁊ eode se man sylf to, þe man tuge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="388" ed="#liebermann"/>We<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Blas_1.lnote.oe.3"/> cwedon be ðam blaseru<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Blas_1.lnote.oe.4"/></hi> ⁊ be ðam morðslihtu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> mon dypte ðone að be ðryfealdu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ⁊ myclade þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ordalisen, ðet hit wǽge ðreo pund, ⁊ eode se man sylf to, ðe man tuge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="389" ed="#liebermann"/>Diximus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Blas_1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> (Dictum est) de blaseriis et murditoribus, ut augeatur iuramentum huius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Blas_1.lnote.oe.4-2"/> abnegationis tripliciter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Blas_1.lnote.oe.5"/>, et maioretur iudiciale ferrum, ut appendat LX sol.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#Blas_1.lnote.oe.dagger"/>, et adeat ipse (homo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Blas_1.lnote.oe.6"/>) compellatus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Blas_1.lnote.oe.7"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-cons"><pb n="389" ed="#liebermann"/>Diximus de balatronibus et de furtiuis mortificatoribus, ut eorum iuramentum et iudiciale ferrum augeatur triplum, ut ponderet III libras, quod accusatus ipse ferat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">We cwædon be þam blaserum and be þam morð-slyhtum, þæt man dypte þone að be þryfealdum and myclade þæt ordalysen, þæt hit gewege<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Blas_1.attnote.fn.2"/> þry pund, and eode se man sylf to, þe man tuge,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="389" ed="#liebermann"/>Wir<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#Blas_1.lnote.de1.dagger"/> haben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Blas_1.lnote.de.1"/> über die Brandstifter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Blas_1.lnote.de.2"/> und über die heimlichen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Blas_1.lnote.de.3"/> Morde bestimmt, dass ihr [Reinigungs]eid ums dreifache<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Blas_1.lnote.de.4"/> erschwert, beziehungsweise<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Blas_1.lnote.de.5"/> das Ordaleisen grösser genommen werde, so dass es 3<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Blas_1.lnote.de.6"/> Pfund wiege; und der verklagte Mann trete selbst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Blas_1.lnote.de.7"/> hinzu [nicht ein Vertreter trage es].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">We [the king and witan] have declared concerning arsonists and secret murders that their [clearing] oath be made three times heavier, or the ordeal iron be made larger so that it weighs 3 pounds; and let the accused man go to it himself [no representative to carry it].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">With regard to incendiaries and those who secretly compass death<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Blas_1.attnote.n.1"/>, we have declared that the oath shall be augmented threefold and the weight of the iron used in the ordeal shall be increased until it weighs three pounds.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#wormald" corresp="#wit-h">We declared about incendaries and underhand killings that the oath be deepened threefold and the ordeal-iron enlarged to a weight of three pounds.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="389"><ref target="clause:IIAs_6">II As 6–6.2</ref>; <ref target="clause:Hu_9">Hu 9</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II As. 6—6, 2 | *vgl. Hu. 9</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="379"><ref target="clause:Hu_8">Hu 8–9</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">The Quadripartitus's ‘LX sol.’ is Norman (compare Hu 9 and Duns 7). Liebermann compares II As 6–6.2. The Consiliatio Cnuti III 1 has another Latin version.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 388, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">388</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Be f. <hi rend="italic">roth</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Be f. in red</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">388</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Engle <hi rend="italic">neuere Hd.; fehlte auch Cons.; doch wohl original</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Engle in a later hand; was also missing in Cons.; but probably original</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">388</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scipe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scipe</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">388</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">d <hi rend="italic">und</hi> t <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">d and t on an erasure.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in <hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> ab <hi rend="italic">Co;</hi> ab <hi rend="italic">OrRMHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in altered to ab Co; ab OrRMHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ra <hi rend="italic">RT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ra RT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ab <hi rend="italic">Or;</hi> a <hi rend="italic">RTMHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ab Or; a RTMHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Normannisch; vgl. Hu.</hi> 9; <hi rend="italic">Duns.</hi> ⁊</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Norman; cf. Hu. 9; Duns. ⁊</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XV <hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> VI <hi rend="italic">Co;</hi> VI <hi rend="italic">OrTMHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XV altered to VI Co; VI OrTMHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aus RTMHk; fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from RTMHk; lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">extra <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">extra Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">c. u. <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. u. Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.de1.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">König und Witan</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">King and witan</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. Einl. 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> Introduction 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Brandstifter 2. 5. <hi rend="italic">Murdrum</hi> und <hi rend="italic">bærnet</hi> bringen gleichen Prozessnachteil Hn 47. Beide sind heimlich; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4a; Mord 2 (<hi rend="italic">clancula occisio</hi> zu II Cn 64 Cons). 4. 6.—Wie hier ‘Mord’ statt ‘Mörder’, so steht Leis Wl 35, 1 ‘Ehebruch’ statt ‘Ehebrecher’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Brandstifter 2. 5. <hi rend="italic">Murdrum</hi> and <hi rend="italic">bærnet</hi> entail the same procedural disadvantage, Hn 47. Both are secret; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4a; Mord 2 (<hi rend="italic">clancula occisio</hi> on II Cn 64 Cons). 4. 6.—Just as ‘murder’ stands here for ‘murderer’, so Leis Wl 35, 1 has ‘adultery’ for ‘adulterer’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Brandstifter 2. 5. <hi rend="italic">Murdrum</hi> und <hi rend="italic">bærnet</hi> bringen gleichen Prozessnachteil Hn 47. Beide sind heimlich; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4a; Mord 2 (<hi rend="italic">clancula occisio</hi> zu II Cn 64 Cons). 4. 6.—Wie hier ‘Mord’ statt ‘Mörder’, so steht Leis Wl 35, 1 ‘Ehebruch’ statt ‘Ehebrecher’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Brandstifter 2. 5. <hi rend="italic">Murdrum</hi> and <hi rend="italic">bærnet</hi> entail the same procedural disadvantage, Hn 47. Both are secret; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4a; Mord 2 (<hi rend="italic">clancula occisio</hi> on II Cn 64 Cons). 4. 6.—Just as ‘murder’ stands here for ‘murderer’, so Leis Wl 35, 1 has ‘adultery’ for ‘adulterer’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Statt <hi rend="italic">abnegationis</hi> in Q⁴ liest <hi rend="italic">negationis</hi> Hs. Rylands von Q Lond.—Grimm <hi rend="italic">DRA</hi> 917 will <hi rend="italic">clypte</hi> ändern: mit Unrecht; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb: deop</hi> letzte Zeile.—Vielleicht hieraus schöpft Hn 66, 9.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Eideshelfer 27; Beweis 8g</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Instead of <hi rend="italic">abnegationis</hi> in Q⁴, the Rylands MS of Q Lond reads <hi rend="italic">negationis</hi>.—Grimm <hi rend="italic">DRA</hi> 917 would emend <hi rend="italic">clypte</hi>: wrongly; <hi rend="italic">see Wb: deop</hi> last line.—Hn 66, 9 perhaps draws on this.—<hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Eideshelfer 27; Beweis 8g</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Wb and</hi> 2, nämlich für die des Eides Unfähigen oder, laut Beweisurteiles, Unwürdigen.—Hieraus oder aus Hu 9 schöpft Hn 64, 1h</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Wb and</hi> 2, namely for those incapable of the oath or, according to the judgment awarding proof, unworthy of it.—Hn 64, 1h draws on this or on Hu 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Eisenordal 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Eisenordal 8</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_1.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd. Gl</hi> Ordal 26.—Das <hi rend="italic">gan to</hi> scheint technisch; Ordal 5¹. Nicht ‘der einen andern anschuldigte’ Grimm</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid. Gl</hi> Ordal 26.—The <hi rend="italic">gan to</hi> seems to be technical; Ordal 5¹. Not ‘der einen andern anschuldigte’ Grimm</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Blas_1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">173</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The Gospels, according to Liebermann.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Blas_1.attnote.n.3" n="3" source="#attenborough" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">171</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">cf. Ine 37, note 1.</seg></note>
